      "extract": "We fix a base ring $\\K$, which is regular noetherian of finite Krull dimension (e.g.\\ a field or $\\Z$). Recall that a commutative $\\K$-ring $A$ is called {\\em essentially finite type} (EFT) if it is a localization of a finite type $\\K$-ring. Note that such a ring $A$ is noetherian and of finite Krull dimension. The category of EFT commutative $\\K$-rings is denoted by $\\cat{Rng} \\eftover \\K$. All rings in this paper",
